'''''Asperula''''', commonly known as '''woodruff''',<ref>{{Cite book|url=http://www.forest.go.kr/kna/special/download/English_Names_for_Korean_Native_Plants.pdf |title=English Names for Korean Native Plants |publisher=[[Korea National Arboretum]] |year=2015 |isbn=978-89-97450-98-5 |location=Pocheon |pages=363 |access-date=25 January 2017 |via=[[Korea Forest Service]] |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170525105020/http://www.forest.go.kr/kna/special/download/English_Names_for_Korean_Native_Plants.pdf |archive-date=25 May 2017 }}</ref> is a [[genus]] of [[flowering plant]]s in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Rubiaceae]]. It contains 91 species and has a wide distribution area from Europe, northern Africa, temperate and subtropical Asia to [[Australasia]].<ref name="WCSP">{{cite web|url=http://apps.kew.org/wcsp/qsearch.do?plantName=Asperula|title=''Asperula'' in the World Checklist of Rubiaceae|access-date=June 10, 2014}}</ref>

